	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Scarlet Monastery rises on the north-eastern heights of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal Glades{/link}, a great house of grey stone behind high walls. It was once a place of learning and prayer, where the priesthood of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} kept its books and trained young paladins in the ways of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link}. Now it is the fortress and the beating heart of the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}. Its bells still ring. Its halls are full of crusaders in red, and none who enter without the Crusade's tabard are welcome.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year the Monastery was founded. Before the plague, it was counted among the proudest seats of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}'s faith, a bastion of knowledge hidden in the glades. Scholars came to its library. Paladins-in-training studied in its halls. When the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} brought the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}, the zealots of the Crusade seized the Monastery and made it a stronghold. They believe that every outsider may carry the plague, and they treat every race but their own as an enemy.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Monastery is the chief bastion of the Crusade in {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}. From here it sends its patrols and messengers to the towers of the glades, and it wages war on the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} at the doors of their own capital. {link:scarlet-commander-mograine}Scarlet Commander Mograine{/link} leads its garrison. Its true master is {link:high-inquisitor-whitemane}High Inquisitor Whitemane{/link}, a priestess who is said to raise the fallen to fight again at her command. In the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}, {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link} wants Whitemane and her chief lieutenants dead. In {link:southshore}Southshore{/link}, {link:raleigh-the-devout}Raleigh the Devout{/link}, who once served here, wants the same. Scholars of both the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} want what is left in the library. The Forsaken want hearts, books and vengeance.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Monastery",
			text = [=[• {b}The Graveyard.{/b} Behind the Monastery lies its burial ground. The Crusade's interrogators work in its crypts, and the restless dead walk among the tombs.
• {b}The Library.{/b} The great library still holds the Monastery's old books, guarded by the Crusade's hound-master and its arcanist.
• {b}The Armory.{/b} Here the Crusade trains its recruits and arms its warriors, under the eye of its champion.
• {b}The Cathedral.{/b} At the heart of the Monastery, {link:scarlet-commander-mograine}Mograine{/link} and {link:high-inquisitor-whitemane}Whitemane{/link} hold the sanctuary of the Crusade.]=],
		},
	},
})

